HuBERT Environment Install
==========================

NOTE:
The pipeline has been tested with:
	- Python 3.10
	- fairseq (local install)
	- CPU-only pytorch
	- Linux

REQUIREMENTS
============

1	PYTHON 3.10
-	-----------
fairseq was not built to work with Python versions higher than 3.10.

2	CONDA
-	-----
Conda is recommended for Python version handling (especially if you
have a newer version installed).

3	PYTORCH 2
-	---------
fairseq seems to only like Torch 2.0.1 and TorchAudio 2.0.2, don't
ask me why, I still haven't figured that out.

INSTALLATION
============

1	CONDA ENVIRONMENT
-	-----------------
You need to create a conda environment as fairseq is not built to work
with any versions of Python newer than 3.10 (thanks facebook).

	$ conda create -n hubert python=3.10
	$ conda activate hubert

2	INSTALL DEPENDENCIES
-	--------------------
Dependencies are in requirements.txt.

	$ pip install -r requirements.txt

3	INSTALL FAIRSEQ
-	---------------
Assuming that you have also cloned the submodules of the repository
(if not, just blame git for your troubles), install fairseq from
external/fairseq:

	$ pip install -e external/fairseq

RUNNING THE PIPELINE
====================

1	PREP LABELS
-	-----------
The following script automatically dumps MFCC features, trains k-means,
generates .km labels, and creates dict.km.txt using the simple_kmeans
pipeline from fairseq:

	$ ./scripts/prepare_hubert_labels.sh

2	LAUNCH HUBERT
-	-------------
Run the train_hubert.sh script:

	$ ./scripts/train_hubert.sh
